NAME='Venus'
COVER_SUB='How you love and what you value in each sign.'
T=[
("Detriment","Venus in Aries is in detriment: love is direct, passionate and impatient. You like the chase, you say what you want and you fall fast. Independence matters, and you can be selfish in romance without meaning to. You are generous when excited and bored when the challenge is gone. The shadow is impulsiveness and conflict mistaken for passion. The lesson: closeness grows after the conquest."),
("Own sign","Venus is at home in Taurus: love is sensual, loyal and patient. You value comfort, beauty, good food, touch and stability, and you build relationships slowly and keep them. Money and pleasure are linked to affection. You are generous and dependable. The shadow is possessiveness and resisting change. The lesson: love is a garden, not a possession."),
("Playful","Venus in Gemini loves with words. You are charming, flirtatious and curious, and conversation is your foreplay. You need variety and an interesting mind more than intensity. Friendship and romance blur easily. The shadow is lightness that avoids depth and a wandering eye. The lesson: staying interested in one person is its own kind of adventure."),
("Tender","Venus in Cancer loves by caring. You are affectionate, protective and loyal, and you need emotional safety before you open up. Home, food and family are the language of love. You remember every kindness and every hurt. The shadow is clinging, moodiness and testing people. The lesson: say what you need instead of waiting to be guessed."),
("Generous","Venus in Leo loves with the whole heart and wants to be adored. You are warm, loyal, romantic and generous with gifts and praise. You like drama, beauty and grand gestures, and you want a partner you can be proud of. The shadow is vanity and needing constant admiration. The lesson: real love can be quiet."),
("Fall","Venus is in its fall in Virgo: love shows through service, attention and small practical acts, but you doubt that you deserve it. You notice flaws and can be shy, critical and hard on yourself. You are loyal, modest and quietly devoted. The shadow is perfectionism in relationships. The lesson: love does not have to be earned flawlessly."),
("Own sign","Venus is at home in Libra: you value harmony, beauty, fairness and partnership. You are charming, diplomatic and happiest in a relationship. Aesthetic taste is a strength, and so is the ability to make others feel at ease. The shadow is avoiding conflict and needing a partner to feel complete. The lesson: choose a partner out of freedom, not fear of being alone."),
("Detriment","Venus in Scorpio is in detriment: love is intense, loyal and all-or-nothing. You want depth, truth and total commitment, and you read your partner closely. Jealousy and control can appear when trust is shaky. Passion transforms you. The shadow is possessiveness and testing. The lesson: intimacy needs trust, not surveillance."),
("Free","Venus in Sagittarius loves freedom, honesty and adventure. You are enthusiastic, humorous and drawn to people who expand your world, often from other cultures. Commitment feels hard when it feels like a cage. The shadow is restlessness and promising more than you can give. The lesson: a good partner is also a good travelling companion."),
("Loyal","Venus in Capricorn is serious about love. You are cautious, loyal and slow to open up, and you value commitment, status and reliability. Affection is shown through effort and responsibility. Love often deepens with age. The shadow is coldness and treating relationships as projects. The lesson: warmth is not a luxury."),
("Friendly","Venus in Aquarius loves as a friend first. You value independence, shared ideals and an unconventional connection, and you are loyal to your friends. Emotional intensity can feel uncomfortable. The shadow is detachment and fear of being tied down. The lesson: a close bond can still leave you free."),
("Exalted","Venus is exalted in Pisces: love is compassionate, romantic and boundless. You are tender, imaginative and willing to forgive almost anything. Music, art and spirituality are part of how you love. You feel other people’s pain as your own. The shadow is idealising, rescuing and self-sacrifice. The lesson: you can love without losing yourself."),
]
